BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-stip-fy-2025-2028-august-revision-20250909@calendars.changes
 aroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T230605Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250909
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Statewide Transportation Improvement Program for FY 2025 - 2
 028 - August Revision
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/statewide/2025/stip-fy
 -2025-2028-august-revision.html
DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - online materials only\; no fixed time (no in-
 person meeting)\nPublic comment deadline: 22 Sep 2025.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: 
 To receive public comments on the August 2025 Revision to Statewide Transp
 ortation Improvement Program (STIP) for FY 2025 - 2028.\n\nDescription: Th
 e STIP reflects the federally funded transportation projects in the FY 202
 5 - 2028 Transportation Improvement Programs (TIPs) for each Metropolitan 
 Planning Organization (MPO) in the state. The STIP includes both state and
  federally funded projects for the nonattainment areas of Dallas-Fort Wort
 h\, El Paso\, Houston and San Antonio. The STIP also contains information 
 on federally funded projects in rural areas that are not included in any M
 PO area\, and other statewide programs as listed.\nTitle 23\, United State
 s Code\, §134 and §135 require each designated MPO and the state\, respe
 ctively\, to develop a TIP and STIP as a condition to securing federal fun
 ds for transportation projects under Title 23 or the Federal Transit Act (
 49 USC §5301\, et seq.). Section 134 requires an MPO to develop its TIP i
 n cooperation with the state and affected public transit operators and to 
 provide an opportunity for interested parties to participate in the develo
 pment of the program. Section 135 requires the state to develop a STIP for
  all areas of the state in cooperation with the designated MPOs and\, with
  respect to non-metropolitan areas\, in consultation with affected local o
 fficials\, and further requires an opportunity for participation by intere
 sted parties as well as approval by the Governor or the Governor's designe
 e.\nA copy of the proposed May August Revision to the FY 2025 - 2028 STIP 
 will be available for review\, at the time the notice of hearing is publis
 hed on the department's website.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.txdot
 .gov/projects/planning/stip.html
CATEGORIES:hearing
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-us290-from-sh130-to-sh95-092325-20250923@calendars.changesar
 oundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T230605Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20250923T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20250923T190000
SUMMARY:TxDOT: US 290 from SH 130 to SH 95 South (Elgin)
LOCATION:Manor Elementary Early Learning Center 12904 Gregg Manor Road Elgi
 n\, TX 78653
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/austin/2025/us290-from
 -sh130-to-sh95-092325.html
DESCRIPTION:In-person meeting\; materials also posted online\nPublic commen
 t deadline: 10 Oct 2025.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: The Central Texas Regional Mob
 ility Authority (Mobility Authority)\, in coordination with the Texas Depa
 rtment of Transportation (TxDOT)\, is considering improvements to US 290 b
 etween SH 130 and SH 95 South (virtual session closed) to increase mobilit
 y and safety along this highly congested corridor.\n\nDescription: An envi
 ronmental study and schematic design is underway to evaluate the extension
  of the 290 Toll from its current end point near SH 130 in Travis County f
 arther east to SH 95 South in Bastrop County\, covering approximately 15 m
 iles. This notice advises the public that TxDOT and the Mobility Authority
  will be conducting a virtual Community Listening Session on the proposed 
 project with two in-person options.\nWhile the proposed improvements will 
 be determined through this study\, TxDOT and the Mobility Authority are co
 nsidering the addition of tolled mainlanes alongside existing non-tolled U
 S 290 general-purpose lanes\, enhancing cross street intersections\, inclu
 ding the possibility of new signals and potential pedestrian and bicycle i
 nfrastructure enhancements where feasible.\nThe proposed project could\, s
 ubject to final design considerations\, require additional right-of-way an
 d potentially displace residential and non-residential structures. Relocat
 ion assistance is available for displaced persons and businesses\, should 
 displacements occur.\nThe proposed project may involve construction in wet
 lands.\nThe proposed project would involve an action in a floodplain.
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
