BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-fm969-corridor-study-100225-20251002@calendars.changesaround
 me.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T230605Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251002T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251002T190000
SUMMARY:TxDOT: FM 969 Corridor Study (Elgin)
LOCATION:Spiderwood Studios 140 Utley Road Elgin\, TX 78621
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/austin/2025/fm969-corr
 idor-study-100225.html
DESCRIPTION:In-person meeting\; materials also posted online\nPublic commen
 t deadline: 3 Nov 2025.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: The purpose of this open house 
 is to share community feedback received during the first open house\, gath
 er input on preliminary improvement options\, and share next steps. In-per
 son open house attendees will be able to review hard copies of project mat
 erials\, ask questions of CAMPO\, TxDOT staff and consultants\, and leave 
 written comments. Online participants will be able to view the same inform
 ation delivered at the in-person public meeting. The virtual meeting will 
 consist of a self-guided virtual meeting room with pre-recorded narration 
 and will include both audio and visual components as well as opportunities
  to provide comments.\n\nDescription: The FM 969 Corridor Study will help 
 CAMPO and TxDOT more clearly define\, identify\, evaluate\, and recommend 
 potential design concepts for FM 969 from SH 130 in East Travis County to 
 SH 71 just west of Bastrop County.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.cam
 potexas.org/local-plans-and-studies/campo-project-readiness-program/fm-969
 -corridor-study/
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-102325-20251023@calendars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T230605Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251023
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Public Transportation Advisory Committee
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/public-transportation/
 2025/102325.html
DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - online materials only\; no fixed time\, mater
 ials post by 10am (no in-person meeting)\n\n—\n\nPurpose: TxDOT invites 
 the public to attend a public meeting of TxDOT’s Public Transportation A
 dvisory Committee (PTAC).\n\nDescription: PTAC is a nine-member legislativ
 ely appointed committee that advises the Texas Transportation Commission a
 bout public transportation-related matters. The committee’s meetings are
  open to the public. The public can listen and view meeting presentations 
 electronically via Teams.\nEach PTAC meeting includes an opportunity for a
 nyone in attendance to address the committee. The Teams meeting\, however\
 , allows attendees to listen/view presentations only. Meeting documents\, 
 including agendas and printed transcripts of previous meetings\, are poste
 d on TxDOT’s PTAC webpage.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.txdot.gov
 /about/advisory-committees/public-transportation-advisory-committee.html
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-102425-20251024@calendars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T230605Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251024
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Bicycle and Pedestrian Advisory Committee Quarterly Meeting
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/public-transportation/
 2025/102425.html
DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - online materials only\; no fixed time\, mater
 ials post by 9:30am (no in-person meeting)\n\n—\n\nPurpose: TxDOT invite
 s the public to attend an in person and virtual public meeting of TxDOT’
 s Bicycle and Pedestrian Advisory Committee.\n\nDescription: TxDOT's Bicyc
 le and Pedestrian Advisory Committee (BPAC) advises the Transportation Com
 mission on bicycle and pedestrian issues to help ensure the bicyclist’s 
 and pedestrian’s perspective will be considered in the development of de
 partmental policies affecting bicycle use and pedestrian activity\, includ
 ing the design\, construction\, and maintenance of roadways. The BPAC is c
 omprised of bicycle and pedestrian enthusiasts who represent various backg
 rounds and perspectives from across the state. Eleven members are selected
  by the Commission to serve voluntary\, three-year terms.\nThe Committee's
  meetings are open to the public. Meeting documents\, including agendas an
 d transcripts of previous meetings\, are posted on TxDOT’s BPAC webpage.
 \n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.txdot.gov/about/advisory-committees/b
 icycle-pedestrian-advisory-committee.html
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-texas-statewide-multimodal-transit-plan-102025-20251113@cale
 ndars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T230605Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251113T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251113T193000
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Texas Statewide Multimodal Transit Plan virtual public meeti
 ng with in-person options
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/public-transportation/
 2025/texas-statewide-multimodal-transit-plan-102025.html
DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - online materials only\; no fixed time\, mater
 ials post by 5pm (no in-person meeting)\nPublic comment deadline: 20 Nov 2
 025.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: As our state’s population and economy continue t
 o grow\, TxDOT has been developing the Statewide Multimodal Transit Plan (
  Texas SMTP 2050 ) to help Texans get to where they want to go more effect
 ively\, efficiently and safely while meeting the needs of our fast-growing
  state and contributing to a next-generation transportation network. With 
 input from stakeholders and communities across the state\, this plan prese
 nts a coordinated\, unified vision for multimodal transportation prioritie
 s through 2050 and beyond. The SMTP includes transit such as buses\, train
 s\, ferries\, and on-demand rideshare. TxDOT is hosting a series of public
  meetings and seeking public feedback on the development of the SMTP.\n\nD
 escription: Between Oct. 22 and Nov. 13\, TxDOT is hosting seven public me
 etings across the state to provide the public information about the Statew
 ide Multimodal Transit Plan ( Texas SMTP 2050)\, ask the technical team qu
 estions about the draft plan\, and provide feedback on the initial priorit
 y steps proposed for implementation.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.t
 xdot.gov/projects/projects-studies/statewide/statewide-multimodal-transit-
 plan.html\n\nMore: https://www.txdot.gov/projects/projects-studies/statewi
 de/statewide-multimodal-transit-plan.html
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
