BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-us77-021926-20260219@calendars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T230605Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260219T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260219T183000
SUMMARY:TxDOT: US 77 from FM 2440 to SH 21
LOCATION:American Legion York Post 276 1502 U.S. 77 Giddings\, TX 78942
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/austin/2026/us77-02192
 6.html
DESCRIPTION:In-person meeting\; materials also posted online\nPublic commen
 t deadline: 23 Mar 2026.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: TxDOT is conducting a schemati
 c and environmental plan for roadway improvements along US 77 from FM 2440
  to SH 21\, a length of approximately eight miles. The purpose of the proj
 ect is to improve safety and enhance mobility for roadway users.\n\nDescri
 ption: The proposed project would widen US 77 from an existing four-lane\,
  undivided highway to a four-lane\, divided highway with a grassy median. 
 The improvements include replacing existing bridges at multiple locations\
 , implementing the Reduced Conflict U-Turn (RCUT) at intersections\, addin
 g new acceleration and deceleration lanes along the corridor\, and constru
 cting a new 10-foot-wide shared-use path on the west side of US 77 from We
 st Independence Street to Giddings High School to accommodate bicyclists a
 nd pedestrians.\nAlthough additional right-of-way would be required\, no r
 esidential or nonresidential structures are anticipated to be displaced at
  this time. Information about services and benefits available to affected 
 property owners\, as well as the tentative schedule for right-of-way acqui
 sition and construction\, may be obtained by calling the Texas Department 
 of Transportation district office at 512-832-7000.\nEnvironmental document
 ation\, maps and drawings showing project location and design\, tentative 
 construction schedules and other information about the proposed project ar
 e available for public inspection Monday through Friday from 8 a.m. to 5 p
 .m. at the TxDOT Bastrop Area Office\, 174 SH 21 E.\, Bastrop\, TX 78602. 
 Project materials also are available on this webpage and in hard copy at t
 he in-person public meeting.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.txdot.gov
 /projects/projects-studies/austin/us77-fm2440-sh21.html
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-mopac-loop1-expressway-ea-030926-20260309@calendars.changesa
 roundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T230605Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260309
SUMMARY:TxDOT: MoPac (Loop 1) Expressway from Cesar Chavez Street to Slaugh
 ter Lane
LOCATION:Austin
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/austin/2026/mopac-loop
 1-expressway-ea-030926.html
DESCRIPTION:In-person meeting\; materials also posted online\nPublic commen
 t deadline: 3 May 2026.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: The purpose of the public heari
 ng is to share the draft EA and Build Alternative\, and receive public com
 ment on the Central Texas Regional Mobility Authority (Mobility Authority)
  and TxDOT’s proposed plan to improve MoPac (Loop 1) Expressway from Ces
 ar Chavez Street to Slaughter Lane in Travis County\, Texas by adding expr
 ess lanes in each direction. Participants may watch a prerecorded video\, 
 view exhibits\, review the proposed schematic\, review the draft Environme
 ntal Assessment and associated technical reports and submit official comme
 nts. Comments must be received or postmarked on or before Sunday\, May 3\,
  2026\, to be included in the official hearing record. For additional info
 rmation\, call 512-342-3299 between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m.\, Monday through Fri
 day\, with questions about the project.\n\nDescription: The Mobility Autho
 rity is proposing to add express lanes along approximately 8-miles of the 
 south MoPac (Loop 1) Expressway from Cesar Chavez Street to Slaughter Lane
  in Austin\, Travis County\, Texas. The Mobility Authority and TxDOT launc
 hed the environmental study in 2013 to identify a mobility solution to thi
 s stretch of congested highway that improves mobility for drivers\, transi
 t riders\, bicyclists and pedestrians in a manner that promotes environmen
 tal stewardship and sustainability.\nIn compliance with Section 4(f) of th
 e Highway Act of 1966 and Chapter 26 Texas Parks and Wildlife Code\, the p
 ublic hearing will present information regarding the temporary constructio
 n easements need to build the project and review potential temporary impac
 ts to park and recreational properties adjacent to MoPac South.
CATEGORIES:hearing
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
